---
import Page from "../../layouts/Page.astro";
import { SlimefootCalculator } from "../../components/SlimefootCalculator.tsx";
---

<Page
  title="Slimefoot Combo Calculator"
  description="Damage / trigger calculator for Slimefoot + Ashnod's Altar + Fresh meat combo in MTG."
>
  <h1>Slimefoot Combo Calculator</h1>
  <p>
    This is a damage / trigger calculator for a Slimefoot-based commander deck
    in Magic the Gathering. There are a few parts to this combo:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <a href="https://gatherer.wizards.com/DOM/en-us/205/slimefoot-the-stowaway">
        Slimefoot, the Stowaway
      </a>{" "}
      (the commander) can create{" "}
      <a href="https://gatherer.wizards.com/DDE/en-us/3/saproling">
        Saprolings
      </a>{" "}
      (1/1 green tokens) for 4 colorless as an activated ability.
    </li>
    <li>
      <a href="https://gatherer.wizards.com/CMM/en-us/368/ashnods-altar">
        Ashnod's Altar
      </a>
      , can sacrifice said Saprolings to generate 2 colorless mana.
    </li>
    <li>
      Slimefoot deals 1 damage to all opponents and heals you for 1 every time a
      Saproling dies.
    </li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    It goes like this: you pile up a bunch of Saprolings, sacrifice them to the
    altar, get mana, deal damage, heal, create more Saprolings, repeat. All of
    this happens at instant speed. Once it starts, it's nearly impossible to
    stop. If someone reacts to this process, you can simply react to them and
    continue.
  </p>
  <p>
    That's the base loop. There's plenty of stuff in the deck that can tweak
    that. Some cards let you create Saprolings on the cheap, some give
    additional effects on Saproling death or on sacrifice.
  </p>
  <!--
    The mb-0 here is to simulate margin collapse. The calculator starts with a
    grid to do a 2 column layout. This creates a Block Formatting Context which
    means that the heading inside that grid can't margin collapse with our
    paragraph here. There's no way to force this so we simulate it instead.
  -->
  <p class="mb-0">
    The following is a calculator that simulates the combo. You put in how many
    Saprolings you start with, how much they cost to create and how long you
    want the simulation to go on for. That last setting is important when the
    cost of creating a Saproling is less than or equal to 2 since the combo goes
    infinite. It then tells you how long it goes on for, how many times
    Slimefoot was triggered and how much mana you have left at the end of it.
    You also get a table that shows you the simulation round by round.
  </p>
  <SlimefootCalculator client:load />
</Page>
